  "id": "COMPOUND:697 - PROTEIN:518",
  "verbalization": "Flurbiprofen is implicated in the target pathway leading to Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Flurbiprofen directly interacts with Protein-arginine deiminase type-3, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Alstonine and Npc126819. These intermediates ultimately converge on Protein-arginine deiminase type-1, indicating a potential cascade of interactions. The shared involvement of Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 as a common target across different compounds supports a mechanism where Flurbiprofen may influence the activity of this enzyme through a downstream pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Flurbiprofen in modulating the activity of this enzyme, possibly through the regulation of its downstream targets. The evidence suggests a plausible mechanism where Flurbiprofen exerts its effects via a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the activation or inhibition of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1.",
